    "body": "### Problem\n\n**Sorry about my title — I don't know how to accurately describe this issue in the title and here.**\nplease see the reproduction below.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n**Test after that PR merged: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41999**\n\ntest.txt\n```test.txt\naaa\n\nbbb\n\nccc\n```\n\ninit.lua\n```init.lua\n_G.test = function()\n\tlocal cursor = vim.fn.getpos(\".\")\n\tlocal anchor = vim.fn.getpos(\"v\")\n\tlocal c_r, c_c, a_r, a_c = cursor[2], cursor[3] - 1, anchor[2], anchor[3] - 1\n\tvim.print((\"mode:%s cursor:{%s, %s}, anchor:{%s, %s}\"):format(vim.fn.mode(), c_r, c_c, a_r, a_c))\n\tvim.cmd.normal({ \"\\27\", bang = true })\n\t-- vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text(0, c_r - 1, c_c + 1, c_r - 1, c_c + 1, { \"@\" })\n\tvim.api.nvim_buf_set_mark(0, \"<\", a_r, a_c, {})\n\tvim.api.nvim_buf_set_mark(0, \">\", c_r, c_c + 1, {})\n\tvim.cmd.normal({ \"gv\", bang = true })\nend\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"x\", \"gm\", \"<cmd>lua _G.test()<cr>\")\n```\n### issue1\nwithout the `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text`:\n1. `:norm! QjjQjjQq=vl`\n2. `gm`, the selection range looks correct:\n\n<img width=\"817\" height=\"592\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/41e2ace7-e944-4482-b591-82a8827105bd\" />\n\n3. `:messages`, The output is a little weird.  I expect there should only be 3 lines of output?\n\n<img width=\"817\" height=\"617\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac1069b9-8e72-4d4d-988d-52c8251456f0\" />\n\n### issue2\nwith `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text`\n1. `:norm! QjjQjjQq=vl`\n2. `gm`, the results looks weird.\n\n<img width=\"817\" height=\"585\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/73398cd5-a932-4725-8529-3b4ebd0b8052\" />\n\nthe result I expect is:\n\n<img width=\"1634\" height=\"1177\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f06280c-58a3-43d6-817a-9b79e2756ae6\" />\n\n3. `:messages`, output:\n\n<img width=\"817\" height=\"617\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1200a4d5-c0f9-47d4-99e4-a8abb1629f74\" />\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nalready been described in the reproduction steps.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-dcf55c0\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n6.18.26.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwindows terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from source",
