            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > issue2\n> \n> A Visual-mode mapping that edits the buffer without ending Visual mode (e.g. `<Cmd>lua vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text(…)<CR>`) makes the selection unreplayable.\n\nA clarification: will this be a known limitation or are there plans to try to fix this (somehow)?\n\n---\n\nAnother example to the collection is the very simplified version of the 'mini.move' \"move visual selection\" mapping: `` vim.keymap.set('x', 'gl', '<Cmd>normal! xp`[1v<CR>') ``. Visually selecting and typing `gl` moves selection to the right (if there is space), but this indeed doesn't work with multicursor.",
